{#
  ONE AD, AS EVERY PLACE DRAWS IT (Services\Ads)

  The anatomy is Meta's feed ad, because it is the one readers already know: who it is from
  and "Sponsored" first, the advertiser's text, the image, then a link bar with the domain,
  the headline and the button. The label sits beside the name at the top left, where the eye
  lands first: the FTC's native-advertising guide asks for exactly that, and warns that a
  label below or apart from the ad is missed. It is a word in the soft ink (4.8:1), never
  pale grey.

  The ⋯ menu carries what every large platform offers on an ad: hide it, report it, why you
  are seeing it, and the advertiser's other ads (the library). Each is a plain form or link,
  so it works with no script; ads.js only makes them answer in place.

  Args (with … only):
    ad          the pick from AdDelivery (or a campaign's ad, for a preview)
    csrf_token  the page's token (`only` hides the global)
    ad.house    our own notice for advertising, drawn when nothing is booked (AdDelivery::
                house()): labelled "From Africa GATES", never "Sponsored", never counted
    preview     true on the advertiser's own pages and the library: nothing is counted,
                the links go straight to the advertiser, and there is no menu
    back        the path the menu's forms return to without a script
    media_box   true to draw the image box even with no image (the builder's live preview)
    wide        true for the homepage band: picture beside the words from 900px up
    ad.own      our own campaign posted by staff (AdStaff): counted like any ad, labelled
                "From Africa GATES", never "Sponsored"
    ad.seen     the views the ad carries on its card ({short, full}; AdDelivery::seenLabel),
                or null below the threshold
    ad.video    a short MP4 over the image (AdVideo), with ad.video_watch the seconds after
                which a play counts as watched

  WHAT MAKES ONE WORTH TAPPING (owner, 4 Nov 2026: "make it more enticing"), from the native
  advertising guidance (IAB, Outbrain, TripleLift, Dable): a picture that carries the
  headline's promise, a short headline, ONE obvious button, and the label above the
  headline. So the button is filled (ink, never the page's green, which belongs to the
  page's own main action), an offer sits ON the picture where the eye already is, and the
  picture leans in slightly under a pointer. The label is untouched: first, at the top.
#}
{% if ad %}
{%- set _house = ad.house|default(false) -%}
{%- set _own = _house or ad.own|default(false) -%}
{%- set _pv = preview|default(false) or _house -%}
{%- set _href = _pv ? ad.url|default('#') : ad.href -%}
{#- Our own notice links our own page, and nobody paid for it, so it is not rel="sponsored". -#}
{%- set _rel = _own ? '' : 'sponsored' ~ (ad.external|default(not (_href starts with '/')) ? ' noopener noreferrer' : '') -%}
<article class="ag-ad{% if wide|default(false) %} ag-ad--wide{% endif %}"{% if not _pv %} data-ad="{{ ad.token }}" data-csrf="{{ csrf_token|default('') }}"{% endif %} aria-label="{{ _own ? 'From Africa GATES'|trans : 'Sponsored: %a%'|trans({'%a%': ad.advertiser}) }}">
  <header class="ag-ad__head">
    {#- With no logo, the site's own monogram (Support\AvatarMark): the advertiser's initials
        on their tone, the way every organisation without a picture is drawn here — a grey
        box with two letters read as a placeholder nobody had filled in. -#}
    {%- set _mk = avatar_mark(ad.advertiser|default(''), null, 'business', 44) -%}
    <span class="ag-ad__logo{% if not ad.logo|default(null) %} ag-ad__logo--{{ _mk.tone }}{% endif %}" aria-hidden="true" data-pv="logo">{% if ad.logo|default(null) %}<img src="{{ ad.logo }}"{% if ad.logo_srcset|default(null) %} srcset="{{ ad.logo_srcset }}" sizes="40px"{% endif %} alt="" width="40" height="40" loading="lazy">{% else %}{{ ad.initials|default('?') }}{% endif %}</span>
    <span class="ag-ad__who">
      <span class="ag-ad__by" data-pv="by">{{ ad.advertiser }}</span>
      <span class="ag-ad__tag">{{ _own ? 'From Africa GATES'|trans : 'Sponsored'|trans }}{% if ad.seen|default(null) %}<span class="ag-ad__seen" title="{{ '%n% views'|trans({'%n%': ad.seen.full}) }}"><svg width="13" height="13" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M2 12s3.5-7 10-7 10 7 10 7-3.5 7-10 7S2 12 2 12z"/><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="3"/></svg>{{ '%n% views'|trans({'%n%': ad.seen.short}) }}</span>{% endif %}</span>
    </span>
    {% if not _pv %}
    <details class="ag-ad__menu">
      <summary class="ag-ad__more" aria-label="{{ 'Options for this ad'|trans }}"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="5" cy="12" r="1.8"/><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="1.8"/><circle cx="19" cy="12" r="1.8"/></svg></summary>
      <div class="ag-ad__pop">
        <form method="post" action="/ads/hide" data-ad-act="hide">
          <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrf_token|default('') }}"><input type="hidden" name="t" value="{{ ad.token }}"><input type="hidden" name="back" value="{{ back|default('/') }}">
          <button type="submit" class="ag-ad__item">{{ 'Hide ad'|trans }}</button>
        </form>
        <details class="ag-ad__sub">
          <summary class="ag-ad__item">{{ 'Report ad'|trans }}</summary>
          <form method="post" action="/ads/report" data-ad-act="report" class="ag-ad__rep">
            <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrf_token|default('') }}"><input type="hidden" name="t" value="{{ ad.token }}"><input type="hidden" name="back" value="{{ back|default('/') }}">
            <fieldset><legend class="ag-ad__lg">{{ 'What is wrong with it?'|trans }}</legend>
              {% for k, label in ad.reasons|default({}) %}<label class="ag-ad__opt"><input type="radio" name="reason" value="{{ k }}"{% if loop.first %} required{% endif %}> {{ label|trans }}</label>{% endfor %}
            </fieldset>
            <button type="submit" class="ag-btn ag-btn--secondary ag-btn--pill ag-ad__send">{{ 'Send report'|trans }}</button>
          </form>
        </details>
        <p class="ag-ad__why"><b>{{ 'Why am I seeing this?'|trans }}</b> {{ 'It is shown to everyone who opens this page. Nothing you did here chose it.'|trans }}</p>
        <a class="ag-ad__item" href="/advertise/library?from={{ ad.id }}">{{ 'More ads from %a%'|trans({'%a%': ad.advertiser}) }}</a>
        <a class="ag-ad__item" href="/advertise">{{ 'About ads on Africa GATES'|trans }}</a>
      </div>
    </details>
    {% endif %}
  </header>
  <p class="ag-ad__text" data-pv="body">{{ ad.body }}</p>
  {%- set _vid = ad.video|default(null) -%}
  {%- set _pic = ad.image|default(null) or _vid or media_box|default(false) -%}
  {#- The offer rides ON the picture when there is one: it is the most clickable fact an ad
      can carry, and the picture is where the eye already is. Outside the hidden picture
      link, so a screen reader reads it. -#}
  {%- set _offer -%}<span class="ag-ad__offer" data-pv="offer"{% if not ad.offer %} hidden{% endif %}>{{ ad.offer }}{% if ad.offer_code %} · <span class="ag-ad__code">{{ ad.offer_code }}</span>{% endif %}</span>{%- endset -%}
  {% if _pic %}
  {#- A VIDEO (Services\Ads\AdVideo) plays inside the same picture link, silently, with the
      image as its poster, in the ad's SHAPE (AdRules::SHAPES: square, upright 4:5, wide 16:9).
      It plays by default, without sound, once ads.js sees it half on screen; nothing is
      fetched before then. With no script, on Save-Data or 2G, or under reduced motion, the
      poster is the ad until somebody presses play. Play/pause is always offered — a clip
      that moves by itself for more than five seconds must be stoppable (WCAG 2.2.2) — and
      sound is one tap. Both sit OUTSIDE the hidden link so they can be reached and named,
      and stay hidden until the script can make them do something. -#}
  {%- set _shape = ad.shape|default('square') -%}
  <div class="ag-ad__media ag-ad__media--{{ _shape in ['portrait', 'landscape'] ? _shape : 'square' }}{% if _vid %} ag-ad__media--video{% endif %}"{% if _vid %} data-ad-video{% if ad.video_watch|default(null) %} data-watch="{{ ad.video_watch }}"{% endif %}{% endif %}>
    <a class="ag-ad__pic" href="{{ _href }}"{% if _rel %} rel="{{ _rel }}"{% endif %} tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true" data-pv="image">{% if _vid %}<video class="ag-ad__vid" muted playsinline loop preload="none" width="600" height="600"{% if ad.image|default(null) %} poster="{{ ad.image }}"{% endif %}><source src="{{ _vid }}" type="video/mp4"></video>{% elseif ad.image|default(null) %}<img src="{{ ad.image }}"{% if ad.image_srcset|default(null) %} srcset="{{ ad.image_srcset }}" sizes="{{ wide|default(false) ? '(min-width: 900px) 360px, ' : '' }}(min-width: 600px) 520px, calc(100vw - 32px)"{% endif %} alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="600" height="600">{% else %}<span class="ag-ad__ph">{{ 'Your image'|trans }}</span>{% endif %}</a>
    {% if _vid %}
    <button type="button" class="ag-ad__vbtn ag-ad__play" data-ad-play hidden aria-label="{{ 'Play the video'|trans }}" data-play="{{ 'Play the video'|trans }}" data-pause="{{ 'Pause the video'|trans }}"><svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true"><path class="ag-ad__i-play" d="M8 5.5v13a1 1 0 0 0 1.5.86l10.5-6.5a1 1 0 0 0 0-1.72L9.5 4.64A1 1 0 0 0 8 5.5z"/><path class="ag-ad__i-pause" d="M7 5h3.5v14H7zM13.5 5H17v14h-3.5z"/></svg></button>
    <button type="button" class="ag-ad__vbtn ag-ad__snd" data-ad-sound hidden aria-pressed="false" aria-label="{{ 'Turn the sound on'|trans }}" data-on="{{ 'Turn the sound on'|trans }}" data-off="{{ 'Turn the sound off'|trans }}"><svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M11 5 6 9H3v6h3l5 4z"/><path class="ag-ad__wave" d="M15.5 8.5a5 5 0 0 1 0 7"/><path class="ag-ad__mute" d="m22 9-6 6m0-6 6 6"/></svg></button>
    {% endif %}
    {{ _offer }}
  </div>
  {% endif %}
  <a class="ag-ad__foot" href="{{ _href }}"{% if _rel %} rel="{{ _rel }}"{% endif %}>
    <span class="ag-ad__meta">
      {#- Where the tap goes, with its kind of place: a chat for WhatsApp (AdRules::displayDomain
          names it so), a link for a website. -#}
      <span class="ag-ad__dom"><svg width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="{{ ad.domain|default('') == 'WhatsApp' ? 'M20 11.5a8 8 0 0 1-11.7 7.1L4 20l1.4-4.1A8 8 0 1 1 20 11.5z' : 'M10 14a4.5 4.5 0 0 0 6.4 0l3-3a4.5 4.5 0 0 0-6.4-6.4l-1 1M14 10a4.5 4.5 0 0 0-6.4 0l-3 3a4.5 4.5 0 0 0 6.4 6.4l1-1' }}"/></svg><span data-pv="domain">{{ ad.domain|default('') }}</span></span>
      <span class="ag-ad__h" data-pv="headline">{{ ad.headline }}</span>
      {% if not _pic %}{{ _offer }}{% endif %}
    </span>
    <span class="ag-btn ag-ad__cta"><span data-pv="cta">{{ ad.cta|trans }}</span><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span>
  </a>
</article>
{% endif %}
